I just made PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104084 to register these editor classes in the correct way. (We can keep that in 4.5 if we want - the code in 4.4 works fine, even if it's using the API incorrectly.)

> And many of those (and maybe others) don't seem to use the `p_level` consistently. Doesn't this actually lead to registering classes multiple times when this is called for each initialization level?

It looks like those only register their classes once. Some just have this at the start of their register function:

```
	if (p_level != MODULE_INITIALIZATION_LEVEL_SCENE) {
		return;
	}
```
